Subject: [PATCH] Avoid embedding build host tool paths

During cross compilation, PATH resolves rustc and cargo to native tools
inside the build sysroot. Embedding those paths leaks build directories
into target binaries and provides unusable runtime fallbacks.

Use tool names instead. Runtime tool discovery already checks rustup
and PATH before consulting these fallback values.

This patch was generated with the assistance of AI.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [cross-compilation specific]

Signed-off-by: Jean-Marc BOUCHE <jean-marc.bouche@foss.st.com>

diff --git a/evcxr/build.rs b/evcxr/build.rs
--- a/evcxr/build.rs
+++ b/evcxr/build.rs
@@ -3,11 +3,6 @@
 fn main() {
     let out_dir = PathBuf::from(std::env::var("OUT_DIR").expect("OUT_DIR must be set"));
 
-    let path = which::which("rustc").expect("Couldn't find rustc on path");
-    let utf8_path = path.to_str().expect("Path isn't valid UTF-8");
-    std::fs::write(out_dir.join("rustc_path"), utf8_path).unwrap();
-
-    let path = which::which("cargo").expect("Couldn't find cargo on path");
-    let utf8_path = path.to_str().expect("Path isn't valid UTF-8");
-    std::fs::write(out_dir.join("cargo_path"), utf8_path).unwrap();
+    std::fs::write(out_dir.join("rustc_path"), "rustc").unwrap();
+    std::fs::write(out_dir.join("cargo_path"), "cargo").unwrap();
 }
